# IntelliROI Project Context

IntelliROI is a multi-tenant B2B SaaS platform that meters, costs, and calculates ROI on
employee AI usage. Frontend stack: Next.js 14+ App Router, React 18, TypeScript (strict),
TailwindCSS, shadcn/ui, TanStack Query, TanStack Table, Zustand, react-hook-form + zod,
recharts.

## Non-negotiable principles

1. **Two pipelines, never merged.** The AI Workspace (chat) is Pipeline 1 — real-time,
   fast, no cost/ROI awareness. Everything under usage/cost/business-context/analytics/roi
   is Pipeline 2 — background, eventually consistent, read-only on the frontend. Never make
   a chat screen wait on a cost or ROI calculation.
2. **Multi-tenancy is structural, not conditional.** Every company-scoped route lives under
   `app/(company)/[companySlug]/`. Never fetch or cache data without the current tenant's
   `company_id` in the query key. Never trust a client-side role check as a security boundary
   — the API enforces RBAC; the frontend only mirrors it for UX.
3. **`app/` contains no business logic.** Pages compose components from `features/` and
   `components/`. If you're writing a `useQuery` call, a zod schema, or a data transform
   directly inside a `page.tsx`, stop and move it into the matching `features/{domain}/`
   folder.
4. **Derived data always shows provenance.** Cost, ROI, and analytics values are
   recomputable — when a formula version or provider pricing changes, they change. Any
   component rendering a `roi_*` or `*_analytics_*` value must be able to show when it was
   last computed and which formula version produced it.
5. **One route, role-adaptive rendering** for shared screens (`/dashboard`, `/analytics`,
   `/roi`, `/usage`) — do not fork these into five separate routes per role. Branch on
   session role inside the page composition instead.

Deep product hierarchy, modules, and MVP scope: skill `intelliroi-architecture`.
